= ACKNOWLEDGEMENT =

Many thanks to the following libraries/resources:

  * Go "sort" package <https://go.dev/src/sort/search.go>
  * Python "bisect" module <https://docs.python.org/3/library/bisect.html>
  * "Algorithms/Sorting/Binary Search" module from GNU libstdc++
     (lower_bound, upper_bound, equal_range namely)
    <https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/libstdc++/latest-doxygen/a01630.html>
  * List::MoreUtils::PP for a large portion of the syntax! :^)
    <https://metacpan.org/dist/List-MoreUtils/source/lib/List/MoreUtils/PP.pm>
  * Ruby "bsearch" method (the "x" variants inspired by Find-any mode)
    <https://docs.ruby-lang.org/en/master/language/bsearch_rdoc.html>
  * RTL binary search (bisectr et al.) from USACO Guide "last_true"
    <https://usaco.guide/silver/binary-search#finding-the-maximum-x-such-that-fx--true>
